# Downloaded faceplate reference photos (source material for hand-authoring the
# panel SVGs). The SVGs we build FROM them are committed; the photos are not.
*-faceplate-reference.*

# Rendered demo narration IS COMMITTED. The web build has no way to render speech — there is no `say`
# in a browser — so an uncommitted set means every demo plays silently for everyone who arrives by
# URL, which is most people. That outweighs the cost, which is real: the render is not byte-stable, so
# a reworded line puts a fresh ~30 kB blob in history and a voice experiment puts the whole set there
# again. `npm run speech` sweeps fragments no script refers to any more, so the folder does not grow
# stale entries — but history keeps what it has already seen. Reword freely; re-render sparingly.
